      "writtenOn": "2026-06-17T06:58:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When it comes to the flag enabled by default (sometime in 160 perhaps), some people may disable the flag because BrotliDecode equally could be a risk (zip bombs, large amounts of data, DOS etc). Hence people may disable it (the same way some people disable JS optimisation from V8 as it also is a common attack surface).\n\nFor the release code to then (when the setting is disabled) go \"Sure thing I\u0027ll parse the brotli\" goes against what the user would want in this case, hence for some reason if the code gets here it should crash regardless of Debug or Release. Hence, I feel it should be a `CHECK()` and not a `DCHECK()`.\n\nCorrect me if I\u0027m wrong here or if the better idea is DCHECK() (realistically speaking though normally if the feature is disabled nothing should even get to BrotliDecoder::Decode)",
      "parentUuid": "7030255e_c2caffe2",
